                    <history>
                        <origin>Produced probably in the <origDate calendar="#Gregorian" notBefore="1601" notAfter="1800">17th or 18th century</origDate>.</origin>
                        <provenance>It was brought from Aleppo, probably between 1750 and 1771, by
                            <name role="fmo" key="person_18003738"><persName>Dr Patrick Russell
                                (1727-1805)</persName></name>, physician and naturalist who
                            worked in Aleppo, Syria and in the Madras Province of India. Dr P.
                            Russell bequeathed it to Mr C. Russell's sons in 1805; see note on the
                            <locus from="Front_paste-down">front paste-down</locus>:
                            <quote>Bequeath'd by Dr Patrick Russell to Mr C. Russell's sons
                                1805</quote> (cf. Van Den Boogert, 2020).</provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>Formerly part of the collection of the Persian scholar <persName
                                    type="standard"
                                    ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/20108923/#Bland,_Nathaniel,_1803-1865"
                                    key="person_20108923" role="fmo">Nathaniel Bland
                                    (1803-1865)</persName>. His bookplate on the <locus
                                    from="Back_paste-down">back paste-down</locus>: "Bland MSS
                                213".</p></provenance>
                        <provenance><p>Bland’s oriental manuscripts were sold through <persName
                                    key="person_5679225" role="bsl">Bernard Quaritch</persName> in
                                1866 to <persName type="standard"
                                    ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/97751058/" key="person_97751058"
                                    role="fmo">Alexander Lindsay, 25th Earl of
                                Crawford</persName>.</p>
                        </provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>
                                <name source="#viaf" key="97751058" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">Alexander Lindsay, 25th Earl of Crawford (1812-1880), book collector and writer on art</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Crawford, Alexander Crawford Lindsay, 1812-1880</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <name source="#viaf" key="9985420" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">James Ludovic Lindsay, 26th Earl of Crawford (1847-1913), astronomer and book collector</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Crawford, James Ludovic Lindsay, Earl of, 1847-1913</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>Formerly in the Crawford Library (Bibliotheca Lindesiana) at Haigh Hall, Lancashire, which was formed and developed by Alexander and James Ludovic Lindsay.</p>
                        </provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>
                                <name  key="person_f6379" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">Enriqueta Rylands (1843-1908), philanthropist and founder of The John Rylands Library</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Rylands, Enriqueta, 1843-1908</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>Purchased by Enriqueta Rylands in <date when="1901">1901</date> from James Ludovic Lindsay, 26th Earl of Crawford (1847-1913).</p>
                        </provenance>
                        <acquisition>
                            <p>Bequeathed by <name role="dnr">
                                <persName type="display">Enriqueta Rylands (1843-1908)</persName>
                                <persName type="standard">Rylands, Enriqueta, 1843-1908</persName>
                            </name> in <date when="1908">1908</date> to <name source="#viaf" key="312795145" role="own">
                                <orgName>The John Rylands Library</orgName>
                            </name>.</p></acquisition>
